{"archetypes":[{"name":"attribution-fidelity","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan uses two distinct label schemes — raw output basenames for code review vs. human-readable `plan_slot_human_label` strings for plan review — and the entire pruning system depends on these labels matching `finding_reviewers` cells in classification TSVs exactly. If they drift, `accepted_count` is always 0 and every combo gets pruned by round 4.","prompt_body":"Examine whether the labels written by `reviewer-prune.sh record` will exactly match the reviewer-attribution strings found in `finding_reviewers` cells of the findings-classification TSVs produced by each skill. For code-review style, check how `normalize_reviewer_label` transforms waterfall output filenames and whether those transformed names match the `label` column `record` would write. For plan-review style, trace `plan_slot_human_label` through `dispatch-plan-review-panel.sh` and `plan-review-loop.sh` to confirm the `--label-map` TSV sent to `record` produces strings that appear verbatim in classification TSV attribution. Identify any transform steps — normalization, fallback re-labelling, archetype renaming — that could produce a mismatch silently at run time. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"ledger-path-threading","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The ledger must be run-stable (shared across all rounds of a single run), but review-core.sh and review-and-fix.sh distinguish IMPLEMENT_TMPDIR (run-stable) from REVIEW_TMPDIR (round-scoped), and the plan's wording is subtly inconsistent about which path is used where.","prompt_body":"For each call site that passes `--prune-ledger` — `review-and-fix.sh`, `review/SKILL.md`, `plan-review-loop.sh` — verify that the ledger file path resolves to the same file across all rounds of a single run and is not inside a round-scoped temp directory that gets recreated or cleaned up between rounds. Check whether `REVIEW_TMPDIR`, `IMPLEMENT_TMPDIR`, and `DESIGN_TMPDIR` have different lifetimes and whether the plan's choice of variable at each call site is consistent with the run-stable requirement. Also verify the plan accounts for `/review` standalone mode, where the tmpdir structure may differ from `/implement`. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"cap-removal-completeness","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan removes degraded-round cap inflation from two files but `count_prior_degraded_rounds` may have additional callers, and MAV/resume math in the loop script uses the effective cap in ways the plan acknowledges need updating — incomplete removal could silently retain the old inflation or introduce dead-code references.","prompt_body":"Verify that `count_prior_degraded_rounds` and `DEGRADED_ROUNDS`/`ROUND_CAP_INFLATED` have no callers or references in scope files beyond the two the plan explicitly targets (`run-step5-review.sh` and `review-implement-step5-loop.sh`). In `review-implement-step5-loop.sh`, trace every place the effective cap is used in MAV-resume and loop-termination logic to confirm the plan's proposed change (replace inflated cap with base cap) is complete without leaving arithmetic that silently produces the wrong cap under degraded conditions. Check whether `skills/implement/SKILL.md` references to degraded-round cap extension are fully covered by the plan's single prose-update note. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
